      "description": "Sirara is a mountain range in the Levant that is to be identified with Mount Hermon (biblical \u1e25erm\u00f4n; modern Gebal a\u0161-\u0160ai\u1e2b; amorite \u015b\u1d49nir), as well as the southern part of Anti-Lebanon mountains (modern Gebal a\u0161-\u0160arq\u012bf). Sirara is mentioned in Assyrian royal inscriptions composed in the reigns of Sennacherib. Esarhaddon, and Ashurbanipal.",
